{
  "choices": [
    {
      "message": {
        "content": "{\n  \"chapter_proposals\": [\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"CH01\",\n      \"title\": \"临床证据格局：抗生素时机、FMT 试验与观察性数据\",\n      \"purpose\": \"评估微生物群扰动与 ICI 结局关联的临床证据强度，区分观察性关联与干预性数据，明确当前转化准备度。\",\n      \"scope\": \"涵盖实体瘤患者中抗生素、PPI 等药物暴露与 ICI 疗效（OS, PFS, ORR）的观察性研究；FMT 及活体生物疗法的早期临床试验数据；排除血液系统恶性肿瘤为主的研究（除非机制可转移）；明确标注缺乏 III 期 RCT 的证据局限。\",\n      \"substantive_threads\": [\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"抗生素暴露的时序效应与剂量反应关系\",\n          \"argument\": \"抗生素对 ICI 疗效的负面影响并非均质，而是高度依赖于给药时机（ICI 启动后 60 天内风险最高）和累积剂量。大样本队列显示 ICI 后暴露与生存劣势关联更强（HR 1.27），提示微生物群在 T 细胞激活关键窗口期的作用，而 ICI 前暴露影响较弱或无显著长期影响。\",\n          \"sources\": {\n            \"redacted\": true,\n            \"original_bytes\": 54,\n            \"sha256\": \"56603e66d0729b302846edb4f0613f259aa448ace37eb2dd909e516cf769a947\"\n          },\n          \"evidence_type\": \"Observational (Retrospective Cohorts)\",\n          \"limitations\": \"回顾性设计无法确立因果；缺乏微生物组直接测量数据作为中介验证；不同研究对抗生素定义（种类、时长）不一致。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"肿瘤类型与治疗方案的异质性调节\",\n          \"argument\": \"抗生素效应在不同实体瘤中存在显著差异：头颈部癌、肾细胞癌和乳腺癌显示显著生存劣势，而肺癌和黑色素瘤在某些大样本分析中未显示统计学意义的生存劣势。这种异质性提示微生物群管理策略需考虑肿瘤生物学特性（如免疫浸润水平）及 ICI 方案（单药 vs 联合）。\",\n          \"sources\": {\n            \"redacted\": true,\n            \"original_bytes\": 54,\n            \"sha256\": \"b798a9c8790814c57edbf772034f8091de1f15188fc39951414a9a0148b18b17\"\n          },\n          \"evidence_type\": \"Observational (Subgroup Analyses)\",\n          \"limitations\": \"亚组样本量限制导致部分癌种统计效力不足；未能完全校正肿瘤突变负荷（TMB）或 PD-L1 状态等混杂因素。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"干预性证据：FMT 试验的疗效与安全性信号\",\n          \"argument\": \"FMT 联合 ICI 在 II 期试验中显示概念验证效力（NSCLC ORR 80%, 黑色素瘤 ORR 75%），但伴随双免疫方案下 irAE 风险显著增加（65% 发生 3 级 +AE）。阴性试验结果（如 MITRIC ORR 0%）表明疗效高度依赖于患者选择（如基线髓系细胞状态）及供体微生物特征，且目前缺乏 III 期 RCT 确证。\",\n          \"sources\": {\n            \"redacted\": true,\n            \"original_bytes\": 54,\n            \"sha256\": \"c8a0706b94db8219d9ab2f439520dbc1d4b3d1f5da3b88eac39c22cbb1036c4c\"\n          },\n          \"evidence_type\": \"Interventional (Phase I/II Trials)\",\n          \"limitations\": \"多为单臂、小样本、无对照组设计；缺乏标准化供体筛选及制备方案；长期安全性数据缺失。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"非抗生素药物的混杂与交互作用\",\n          \"argument\": \"PPI、类固醇及阿片类药物使用与 ICI 疗效下降相关，可能通过微生物群介导或独立免疫抑制机制。PPI 效应具有时间依赖性（基线长期使用风险高），且可能与化疗存在交互（化疗可能抵消 PPI 影响）。这些药物作为关键混杂因素，需在评估微生物群独立效应时严格控制。\",\n          \"sources\": {\n            \"redacted\": true,\n            \"original_bytes\": 54,\n            \"sha256\": \"e00549e61b7e71424a5e14d70d1f546e50d2a5733ff177ccb83e6db7b8b98a52\"\n          },\n          \"evidence_type\": \"Observational (Meta-analyses & Cohorts)\",\n          \"limitations\": \"适应症偏倚（病情重者更常用药）；缺乏微生物组数据验证中介机制；不同药物类别效应异质性大。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"证据等级综合与转化瓶颈\",\n          \"argument\": \"当前临床证据主要由观察性数据和早期干预试验构成，缺乏 III 期 RCT 支持。抗生素管理可基于观察性数据提出谨慎建议，但 FMT 及代谢物干预因标准化缺失及安全性信号（如 irAE 交互），尚不能作为标准治疗推荐。未来需优先开展标准化 RCT 及微生物组定量监测。\",\n          \"sources\": {\n            \"redacted\": true,\n            \"original_bytes\": 54,\n            \"sha256\": \"5485c8277f67b49f8fba21957931ceffe338cc034448bc597b0124b2ef8b84a3\"\n          },\n          \"evidence_type\": \"Synthesis (Reviews & Surveys)\",\n          \"limitations\": \"本次检索确认无已完成的大规模 III 期 RCT；方法学异质性（测序、定义）阻碍结果比较；临床医生认知与证据现状存在差距。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"excluded_source_handles\": [\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0272\",\n          \"reason\": \"聚焦血液系统恶性肿瘤（CAR-T/ICI），机制与实体瘤微环境差异大，且无微生物组数据，仅作为背景对比排除。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0094\",\n          \"reason\": \"仅定义超进展（HPD）表型，无微生物组数据，不能用于推导微生物机制，仅作为背景排除。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0167\",\n          \"reason\": \"聚焦生活质量（QoL）而非微生物组或 ICI 疗效的直接调节，虽确立 ICI 获益基线但无微生物相关数据，排除。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0226\",\n          \"reason\": \"聚焦放疗联合 ICI，无微生物组数据，虽量化联合治疗基线但无法回答微生物调节问题，排除。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0256\",\n          \"reason\": \"仅确立 TNBC 中 ICI 疗效基线，无微生物组数据，不能用于推导微生物调节机制，排除。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0259\",\n          \"reason\": \"仅报告皮肤毒性发生率，无微生物组数据，不能用于回答微生物调节问题，排除。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"supplement_requests\": [],\n      \"directed_reads\": [\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0575\",\n          \"instruction\": \"重点提取按肿瘤类型分层的 HR 值及置信区间，特别是肺癌与黑色素瘤亚组无显著性的具体统计量，用于论证异质性。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n          \"instruction\": \"详细记录 FMT-LUMINate 试验中 NSCLC 与黑色素瘤队列的 ICI 方案差异（单药 vs 双药）及对应的 irAE 发生率，用于论证安全性与方案的交互作用。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n          \"instruction\": \"提取 MITRIC 试验中基线生物标志物（如髓系细胞）与临床获益的关联数据，用于讨论患者选择对 FMT 疗效的影响。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"transition_logic\": \"本章确立了微生物群扰动（抗生素）与 ICI 结局的临床关联及 FMT 干预的早期信号，但未阐明具体是哪些微生物特征介导了这些效应。下一章（CH02）将深入分析响应者与无响应者之间的特定菌分类群及代谢物差异，从‘是否有关联’转向‘什么特征在调节’。\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"screened_sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0272\",\n      \"reason\": \"聚焦血液系统恶性肿瘤（CAR-T/ICI），机制与实体瘤微环境差异大，且无微生物组数据，仅作为背景对比排除。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0094\",\n      \"reason\": \"仅定义超进展（HPD）表型，无微生物组数据，不能用于推导微生物机制，仅作为背景排除。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0167\",\n      \"reason\": \"聚焦生活质量（QoL）而非微生物组或 ICI 疗效的直接调节，虽确立 ICI 获益基线但无微生物相关数据，排除。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0226\",\n      \"reason\": \"聚焦放疗联合 ICI，无微生物组数据，虽量化联合治疗基线但无法回答微生物调节问题，排除。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0256\",\n      \"reason\": \"仅确立 TNBC 中 ICI 疗效基线，无微生物组数据，不能用于推导微生物调节机制，排除。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0259\",\n      \"reason\": \"仅报告皮肤毒性发生率，无微生物组数据，不能用于回答微生物调节问题，排除。\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "The user wants a chapter proposal for Chapter 1 (CH01) of a review on the gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) in solid tumours.\nThe chapter title is \"临床证据格局：抗生素时机、FMT 试验与观察性数据\" (Clinical Evidence Landscape: Antibiotic Timing, FMT Trials, and Observational Data).\nThe purpose is to evaluate the strength of clinical evidence linking microbiome perturbation to ICI outcomes, distinguishing observational associations from interventional data.\nThe scope adjustment notes that no Phase III RCTs were found, so limitations must be clearly marked. Antibiotic timing data is complete enough to distinguish pre- vs. post-ICI exposure effects.\n\nI need to structure the chapter proposal with:\n- chapter_id\n- title\n- purpose\n- scope\n- substantive_threads (ordered themes with specific source handles and argumentation logic)\n- excluded_source_handles (if any, with reasons)\n- supplement_requests (if any, with gap_id, gap_question, success_criteria, intended_use, targeted_queries)\n- directed_reads (if any)\n- transition_logic (how this chapter connects to the next)\n\nKey constraints from the system prompt:\n- Do not write a Q&A list.\n- Organize by research question, disciplinary context, and existing material.\n- Do not assume a single paradigm.\n- Center on the user's research question.\n- Distinguish association vs. causation, mechanism vs. explanation, migration vs. application, validation vs. uncertainty.\n- Do not upgrade unmet needs to field-level lack judgments.\n- Preserve source metadata (source_handle).\n- Use the provided source_routing ledger.\n- Correct overclaims in the L1 outline based on routed evidence.\n- Return JSON only.\n\nKey evidence from source_routing for CH01:\n- Large observational cohorts (Zhang et al., n=21,108) on antibiotic timing (P0575).\n- FMT trials (FMT-LUMINate, n=40) (P0197, P0583, P0586).\n- Multiple retrospective antibiotic exposure studies (P0007, P0035, P0039, P0052, P0061, P0068, P0100, P0107, P0135, P0185, P0236, P0310, P0345, P0402, P0418, P0470, P0547, P0564, P0576).\n- No Phase III RCTs confirmed (tool material).\n- Antibiotic timing effects vary by tumor type (P0575).\n- FMT safety signals (irAEs) vary by ICI regimen (P0197, P0583).\n\nSubstantive threads should cover:\n1. Observational evidence of antibiotic exposure (timing, dose, class) and ICI outcomes (OS, PFS, ORR).\n2. Tumor type heterogeneity in antibiotic effects.\n3. Interventional evidence from FMT trials (efficacy, safety, donor factors).\n4. Other medication effects (PPIs, opioids, steroids) as confounders or modifiers.\n5. Limitations of current evidence (observational nature, lack of Phase III, standardization issues).\n\nI need to ensure I don't overclaim causality for observational data.\nI need to explicitly state the lack of Phase III RCTs as a limitation of the evidence, not necessarily a field-wide absence (though the tool material says \"confirmed_absence\" for completed large-scale Phase III RCTs in the context of the search).\nI need to use specific source handles in the substantive_threads.\n\nLet's draft the substantive_threads:\n1. Antibiotic Exposure and ICI Outcomes: Timing and Dose-Response.\n   - Focus on Zhang et al. (P0575) for timing (pre vs post).\n   - Focus on meta-analyses (P0039, P0052, P0068, P0236, P0345) for overall effect size.\n   - Focus on dose/duration (P0061, P0107, P0360).\n2. Tumor-Type Specificity of Antibiotic Effects.\n   - Focus on Zhang et al. subgroups (P0575) (HNC, RCC, Breast vs Lung, Melanoma).\n   - Focus on specific cancer reviews (P0090 for RCC, P0113 for HCC, P0275 for HCC negative result).\n3. Interventional Evidence: FMT Trials.\n   - Focus on FMT-LUMINate (P0197, P0583, P0586) for ORR and safety.\n   - Focus on MIMic (P0577) and MITRIC (P0578) for comparison (positive vs negative results).\n   - Highlight the difference between single-arm Phase II and lack of Phase III.\n4. Confounding Medications and Host Factors.\n   - PPIs (P0007, P0135, P0185, P0339, P0537).\n   - Opioids/Steroids (P0016, P0007).\n   - Host factors (Age, Performance Status) (P0181, P0376).\n5. Synthesis of Evidence Strength and Limitations.\n   - Observational vs Interventional.\n   - Lack of Phase III (tool material).\n   - Standardization issues (P0026, P0103).\n\nExcluded sources:\n- Sources that are purely mechanistic without clinical data (better for CH03).\n- Sources that are purely about biomarkers without outcome data (better for CH02).\n- Sources that are about hematological malignancies unless relevant for comparison (P0272).\n- Sources that are purely about diet without ICI outcome data (better for CH04).\n\nSupplement requests:\n- The tool material already confirmed the absence of Phase III RCTs. I might not need a supplement request for that unless I want to check for *ongoing* trials that might change the landscape soon, but the instruction says \"limited supplementary search... does not equal field-level lack judgment\". I should probably not request a supplement for something already confirmed as absent in the search, but rather frame it as a limitation.\n- However, I might need to check if there are any *published* Phase III results that were missed, but the tool material says \"Based on the reviewed materials, there are no completed large-scale Phase III randomized controlled trials\". I will accept this as the current state.\n- I might want to ask about specific antibiotic classes if the current data is too aggregated, but the prompt says \"evidence sufficient... do not force sources\". The current data on classes is limited (P0376 mentions fluoroquinolones). I can note this as a limitation without a supplement request if the search didn't yield more.\n- Actually, the instruction says \"Every supplement_requests entry must include...\". If I don't need supplements, I can leave the list empty or omit the key. But usually, there's some gap. The gap is \"specific antibiotic class effects\" or \"standardized FMT protocols\". Let's see if I need to request more. The prompt says \"Evidence sufficient... do not force\". I think the current material is sufficient to write the chapter about the *state* of evidence. I will not add supplement requests unless I find a critical gap that prevents writing the chapter's argument. The lack of Phase III is a conclusion, not a gap preventing writing.\n- Wait, the instruction says \"Return chapter_proposals... and screened_sources\". I need to make sure I include screened_sources if I exclude any.\n- I will focus on the structure.\n\nTransition logic:\n- CH01 establishes the clinical associations (antibiotics bad, FMT promising but early).\n- CH02 will dive into the specific microbial features (which bugs?) associated with these outcomes.\n- Transition: \"Having established that microbiome perturbation correlates with ICI outcomes, we next examine the specific taxonomic and metabolic signatures...\"\n\nLet's refine the substantive_threads to be more argumentative.\nThread 1: The Antibiotic Signal - Timing and Magnitude.\nThread 2: Context Matters - Tumor Type and Regimen Heterogeneity.\nThread 3: From Association to Intervention - FMT Trial Results.\nThread 4: The Confounder Landscape - PPIs, Steroids, and Host Status.\nThread 5: Evidence Grading - What is Missing for Clinical Implementation.\n\nI need to make sure I use the source_handles provided in the routing.\nP0575 (Zhang et al.) is crucial for timing.\nP0583 (FMT-LUMINate) is crucial for FMT efficacy.\nP0578 (MITRIC) is crucial for FMT negative results.\nP0039, P0052, P0068, P0236, P0345 are meta-analyses for antibiotic effect.\nP0135, P0185, P0339 for PPIs.\n\nI will write the JSON now.",
